>> title: White Cut Chicken
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, chinese, poached, cold plate, ginger
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter, One Pot, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: bak chit gai, baak cit gai, 白切雞, white cooked chicken, poached chicken, plain chicken
>> pairs-with: ginger-scallion-oil
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 30 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the pot has to be big enough and hot enough to carry the bird through: an under-poached chicken is a safety failure

>> step: poach 30 min off the heat, lid on
Poach @whole chicken{3 1/2%lb}(1.6 kg) breast-down in a #stockpot{} of @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) boiled with @fresh ginger{6%slices}(coin-sized), @scallions{3}(knotted) and @kosher salt{2%Tbs}: back to a tremble, lid on, off the heat altogether, ~poach{30%min}.

>> step: chill in an ice bath 15 min, until the skin draws tight
Lift @&(~1)chicken{} straight into @iced water{4%qt}(3.8 L; half of it ice) and ~chill{15%min}.

>> step: rest 20 min, rub with sesame oil, chop
Drain @&(~1)chicken{}, ~rest{20%min} on a rack, rub it over with @toasted sesame oil{2%tsp}, and chop it through the bone.
